      {
        "id": 218733,
        "name": "Blackfang108",
        "username": "Blackfang108",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/b/74df32/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2018-06-11T19:01:43.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"PlatinumWarlock\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/platinumwarlock/48/1869_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> PlatinumWarlock:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>Trajector wrote:</b><br><blockquote>Ah, that is a dangerous point to reach... My family found and kept a snapping turtle for a while, until it started ignoring the worms we fed it in favor of the fingers holding the worms. Then we let it go into the pond where we found it.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nFor what it's worth, beardies are much less aggressive (and much less carnivorous; they're omnivores) than snapping turtles.&nbsp; Even if they did grab a finger, they'd likely freak out and immediately let go, rather than chomping down.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Pretty much.&nbsp; He's bit my wife a total of… three times?&nbsp; Never so much as broke the skin.</p>",
        "post_number": 24,
